==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
First attested [[w:1382|1382]], from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|cocatriz|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|calcatrix|calcātrīx|she who treads upon something|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|calco|calcō|tread|lang=la}}, from {{term|calx|calx|heel, hoof|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A legendary creature about the size and shape of a [[dragon]] or [[wyvern]], but in appearance resembling a giant [[rooster]], with some lizard-like characteristics.
#* {{rfdate}} [[w:J. Walker McSpadden|J. Walker McSpadden]], ''The Spell of Egypt''
#*: ''“Peace reigns in happy Luxor. The lion lies down with the lamb, and the child, if it will, may harmlessly put its hand into the '''cockatrice’s''' den”''

